    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0635" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Saigon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Abbott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-12T12:00:00+08:00">December 12,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 12—7:08 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>437. Following signed statement issued [by] Pignon<anchor n="9" xml:id="d721-f1"
                    /> over weekend: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Am authorized by French and Vietnam Governments announce following
                            position:</p>
                        <p>French and Vietnam Governments feel need announce their position in case
                            Chinese military formations should be tempted to try penetration
                            Indochina, particularly Vietnam. Instructions given <pb facs="0636"
                                n="626" xml:id="pg626"/> troops French Union are to oppose entry
                            Indochina any foreign troops which appear at frontier under arms. If
                            such case occurs elements which cross frontier will be ejected or
                            disarmed and interned. In no case will French and Vietnam Governments
                            permit Vietnam or other French Union territory be used as refuge by
                            elements which might influence security frontier region or good
                            neighborly relations with border states.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Evident Pignon not as confident on border situation as his press condemn Bao Dai
                    departure indicated (Contel 436, December 12).<anchor n="10" xml:id="d721-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Pouched Hanoi. Department pass Paris, Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abbott</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d721-f1" n="9" xml:id="d721-f1-content">
                <p>Leon M. Pignon, French High Commissioner in Indochina.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d721-f2" n="10" xml:id="d721-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; Bao Dai, Chief of State of Vietnam since June 14, 1949, departed for
                    France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
